{
  "description": "Three platform adapters use HTTP APIs for bulk data loading but hardcode http://\nwith no option for HTTPS:\n\n1. **QuestDB** (PR #28): REST API for /imp endpoint - questdb.py:348, 382\n2. **Doris** (PR #30): Stream Load API - doris.py:418, 443-448\n   Also sends credentials via HTTP Basic Auth in plaintext.\n3. **Databend** (PR #29): DSN construction - databend/adapter.py:256-258\n   Password not URL-encoded either (separate issue).\n\nFor localhost/Docker development, HTTP is fine. But for remote or cloud deployments,\ncredentials and data are transmitted in cleartext. This is a security concern for\nproduction use.\n\nThe fix should add a use_tls or http_scheme configuration option to each adapter,\ndefaulting to http:// for backward compatibility but allowing https:// for remote\ndeployments.",
